File: lilypond-internals.info,  Node: ArticulationEvent,  Next: BarCheckEvent,  Prev: ArpeggioEvent,  Up: Music expressions

1.1.9 ‘ArticulationEvent’
-------------------------

Add an articulation marking to a note.

   Syntax: NOTE‘x’‘y’, where ‘x’ is a direction (‘^’ for up or ‘_’ for
down), or LilyPond’s choice (no direction specified), and where ‘y’ is
an articulation (such as ‘-.’, ‘->’, ‘\tenuto’, ‘\downbow’).  See the
Notation Reference for details.

   Event classes: *note articulation-event::, *note music-event::, *note
script-event:: and *note StreamEvent::.

   Accepted by: *note Beat_engraver::, *note Beat_performer::, *note
Drum_note_performer::, *note Note_performer::, *note Script_engraver::
and *note Toe_heel_engraver::.

   Properties:

     ‘name’ (symbol):
          ‘'ArticulationEvent’

          Name of this music object.

     ‘types’ (list):
          '(post-event
             event
             articulation-event
             script-event)

          The types of this music object; determines by what engraver
          this music expression is processed.


File: lilypond-internals.info,  Node: BarCheckEvent,  Next: BarEvent,  Prev: ArticulationEvent,  Up: Music expressions

